{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/stigma",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "stigma"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "The structural and societal imposition of negative stereotypes, prejudices, and harmful practices relating to a certain category of persona. These grounds are perceived to distinguish the person or group from other members of society. Stigma can be affixed to a person by society if they differ from cultural norms."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "In the context of women with disabilities, stigma operates as an intersectional barrier where stereotypes about both gender and impairment overlap. This process fosters social exclusion, increases exposure to gender-based violence, and acts as a safeguarding failure that restricts access to justice and protective support networks. Within this human rights framework, tackling stigma is recognised as an essential prerequisite to achieving 'respect for inherent dignity, individual autonomy, and full inclusion in society', as stigma directly drives the multiple and intersectional forms of discrimination and violence faced by girls and women with disabilities"
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "6.11"
  ],
